{"candidates":[{"checker_specs":[],"claim":"Four straight cuts, each passing through the exact center of the pizza, produce exactly 8 pieces.","counterconditions":["If one or more cuts do not pass through the exact center (general position), the number of regions increases.","If cuts are not straight, the region count depends on the curvature and intersections of the cuts."],"evidence_refs":[],"mechanism":"Because every cut passes through the center, they form 4 concurrent lines intersecting at a single point. Each distinct line adds 2 new regions, so n concurrent lines yield 2n regions. For n=4, this gives 8 regions.","optional_refs":["5374c535f21d37f9175372076fb946e73dbe6f6fe8204b6c82d7240572cc43f2","ba408a0b043737d7180e6612af0ed40b0daa182cc699a38437bdb9f74b0c7d66","86d4a9754db70cbda28f527ba56d25631dd1d2d3960f64b578558f900e02e8c8","d651ad297b18c9c1643fd253f2e0b9cd86c4812ec58018c6368cdc8ff1d91b89"],"sidecar":{"requested_context_aliases":[],"search_signal":"productive"},"typicality":0.95},{"checker_specs":[],"claim":"If the four straight cuts are assumed to be in general position rather than concurrent, they produce a maximum of 11 pieces.","counterconditions":["If the cuts are constrained to pass through the exact center, they become concurrent and the number of regions drops to 8.","If some cuts are parallel or concurrent, the number of regions is less than 11."],"evidence_refs":[],"mechanism":"The lazy caterer's sequence gives the maximum number of regions for n lines in a plane as R(n) = n(n+1)/2 + 1. For n=4, R(4) = 11. This is a known trap if the solver ignores the 'exact center' constraint and treats the cuts as generic lines.","optional_refs":["ef6203d5fde706109d10717675809f7b1076d826fb78368ab6054939716e7109","86d4a9754db70cbda28f527ba56d25631dd1d2d3960f64b578558f900e02e8c8","c7c20604671599f7e97da06102eaaec5a9bcd17f4a3a1e6652b4195d299be858"],"sidecar":{"requested_context_aliases":[],"search_signal":"productive"},"typicality":0.3},{"checker_specs":[],"claim":